{
  "description": "The Scope Registry — the single source of truth for which persistence tables are SCOPE-OWNED (belong to a bounded scope such as an organization) versus intentionally global. The repository tenant-scope guard (roadmap M8.2, AM-7) and its CI gate read this file. Tables NOT listed are global and carry no scope predicate (identity, sessions, credentials, tenancy, audit, outbox). Extensible by design: a table declares a list of `scopes` (scopeType + soft-ref column), so future scope types (facility, department, care-circle, household, employer, insurer, government-region, research-cohort, future workspace types) are additive — add a scopeType and the scope binding, no redesign. Today the only live scopeType is `organization`.",
  "scopeTypes": {
    "live": ["organization"],
    "reserved": [
      "facility",
      "department",
      "care-circle",
      "household",
      "employer",
      "insurer",
      "government-region",
      "research-cohort"
    ]
  },
